Cross build support files for musl-linux-wasm32, as Debian has them for
each of its ports in debian/cross/ARCH: perl's own Configure run as a native
build with the wasm32 compiler (its test programs run under gexc), the
build paths and the build machine's library paths taken out, and no C11
thread-local interpreter pointer (d_thread_local): an XS module refers to
PL_current_context in perl, and wasm-ld has no TLS relocation against a
symbol another module defines, so perl keeps it in pthread_getspecific as
it does where the compiler has no _Thread_local.

